> ChaTraMue brand preferred gives authentic flavor and orange color
> Sweetened condensed milk creates creamy sweetness and richness
> Evaporated milk or heavy cream for smooth texture
> Salt enhances all flavors naturally

== Brew the Tea Strong ==

Boil @water{4%cups} in #large pot{}. Add @Thai tea mix{4%tablespoons} and let steep for ~{8-10%minutes}. Don't make it weak or it tastes like orange water. Strain out all tea leaves with #fine mesh strainer{}.

== Sweeten While Hot ==

Stir in @sugar{1/3%cup}(adjust to taste preference) and @salt{1%pinch} while tea is still hot so it dissolves completely. Add @?orange food coloring{} if desired. Let cool to room temperature.

== Mix the Creamy Layer ==

In separate #bowl{}, whisk together @sweetened condensed milk{1/2%cup} and @evaporated milk{1/4%cup} until smooth. Should look creamy and well combined without lumps.

== Serve and Layer ==

Fill glasses with @crushed ice{4%cups} and pour tea over. Top with the creamy milk mixture.